# Moxa ioLogik R1210.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Moxa ioLogik R1210 Remote RTU I/O — 16-channel DI
# | 
# | Source: ioLogik R1200 Series User Manual V3.2, November 2017 (Appendix)
# | Protocol: Modbus RTU (RS-485); 9600 8N1 default, address configurable via software
# | 
# | DI channels (ch0-15):
# | FC03 addr 0x0000-0x000F (0-15): DI Mode ch0-15 (0=DI, 1=Counter)
# | FC03 addr 0x0020-0x002F (32-47): DI filter value ch0-15
# | FC03 addr 0x0040-0x004F (64-79): DI counter trigger type (0=L2H, 1=H2L, 2=Both)
# | FC04 addr 0x0000-0x000F (0-15): DI value word ch0-15
# | FC04 addr 0x0020, 0x0022... (32,34,36...62): DI counter value ch0-15 (u32, 2 words/ch, step 2)
# | FC02 addr 0x0000-0x000F (0-15): DI bit value ch0-15
# | FC01 addr 0x0000-0x000F: DI counter start; addr 0x0020: DI counter reset;
# | addr 0x0040: DI counter overflow; addr 0x0060: DI power-on counter start;
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Moxa
@model=ioLogik R1210
@description=16-DI remote RTU I/O, Modbus RTU RS-485 9600 8N1. FC03: DI_Mode ch0-15 (0-15, 0=DI 1=Counter), DI_filterValue ch0-15 (32-47), DI_counterTriggerType ch0-15 (64-79, 0=L2H 1=H2L 2=Both). FC04: DI_value ch0-15 (0-15), DI_counterValue u32 ch0-15 (32,34,...62 step-2 pairs). FC02: DI_bitValue ch0-15 (0-15). FC01: DI_counterStart (0-15), DI_counterReset (32-47), DI_counterOverflow (64-79), DI_powerOnCounterStart (96-111), DI_safeModeCounterStart (128-143), DI_powerFailingCounterStorage (160-175).
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/moxa-iologik-r1210.toml; Source: ioLogik R1200 Series User Manual V3.2, November 2017 (Appendix). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

